    "blurb": "The set opens with a driving Truckin' that sets a high‑energy tone. Dark Star segues into an emotive Morning Dew highlighted by Jerry’s soaring lead and dual keyboards, while It Hurts Me Too and Good Lovin’ showcase the tight rhythm section. The performance is crisp, balanced, and ranks among the stronger Europe ’72 dates.",
    "review": "The May 18, 1972 concert at Kongressaal Deutsches Museum captures the Dead in full flight. From the first note of Truckin' the band launches into a high‑octane groove that never lets up, spilling into a set packed with tight jams and melodic excursions. Highlights include a soaring Dark Star that morphs seamlessly into an emotionally charged Morning Dew—Jerry’s guitar tone is described as stupendous while Keith’s piano duels playfully with Pigpen’s organ, creating a gorgeous dual‑keyboard texture. It Hurts Me Too brings out a soulful vocal from Garcia paired with Phil’s ‘bomb’ of bass work, and Good Lovin' (Pigpen) showcases the group’s tight interplay and energetic vocals. The rhythm section—Billy’s tasteful drum breaks and powerful groove—holds everything together, making this one of the most compelling Europe ’72 recordings available.",
